-label pi-secondary-font\">Version</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"implementation-date\">7.8<br/>August 1, 2006<br/>Summer Update 2006</span></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><p>\t    See also: Hunting Places <span class=\"explained\">Help</span></p></nav>\n</aside>\n<p><b>Nargor</b> is the second largest island in the <a href=\"#/wiki/Shattered%20Isles\">Shattered Isles</a>. The island is surrounded by jagged reefs and mountains, making it particularly difficult to reach. This provides a distinct advantage to the skilled sailors that call themselves <a href=\"#/wiki/Pirates\">Pirates</a>.\n</p><p>Nargor is home to the largest known pirate base, and the island is riddled with caves and traps to prevent unauthorized access. There is also a <a href=\"#/wiki/Nargor%20Undead%20Cave\">cave</a> haunted by a couple of undead pirates.\n</p><p>Accessed via the <a href=\"#/quest/the-shattered-isles-quest\">Meriana Quest</a>.<br/>\nIf you have completed the quest, you can get to Nargor by going to <a href=\"#/wiki/Liberty%20Bay\">Liberty Bay</a>, using the password \"peg leg\" with <a href=\"#/wiki/Captain%20Waverider\">Captain Waverider</a> and asking <a href=\"#/wiki/Sebastian\">Sebastian</a> to bring you to Nargor.\n</p><p><br/>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable full-width\"><caption>Nargor NPCs (4 NPCs)</caption><tbody><tr><th>Name</th><th class=\"npc-animation\" style=\"width: 128px; text-align: center;\"></th><th style=\"width: 110px; text-align: center;\">Job</th><th style=\"width: 72px; text-align: center;\">Buy/Sell</th><th style=\"\">Location</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 100px;\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Klaus\">Klaus</a></td><td class=\"npc-animation\" style=\"width: 128px; text-align: center; line-height: 64px;\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Klaus\"><img alt=\"Klaus\" class=